jitContinueRT -- SEQ 409 R2 (2026-10-23), a find pinned before it is chased: A HANDED-OVER `continue` IS DROPPED. pcWalk is
compiled; its loop body's `if *pcCur["mark"]; continue;` is handed to run time (an operator with no emitter), and jitStmtRT
honours only a `return` (branchKind 3, SEQ 393 A) -- a `continue` (2) or a `break` (1) run there is cleared and lost, so the
compiled loop falls through to `pcN = pcN + 1` for the marked member too. PC-1 reads 3 where the interpreted twin
(`jitter;` -> `jitterOff;`) reads 2; built 1 called 1, silent. On trunk's binary and on jit-seed-scope-a alike. It is the
second mechanism behind the compiled generator's runaway: walkRules' `if *grup["pendingParseR"]; continue;` is this shape.

Intended: PC-1 = the twin's 2.
